From 17c082a36c4ed4ef631a23e3659b6125d6fd463f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ville=20Kivel=C3=A4?= <vkivela@hotmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:25:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] extensions: let the application say which tab the reader
 selected

tabs.query({ active: true }) answered the last page on show in the
profile, the only guess the engine could make. Two pages are on show at
once in a split, or in two windows, and the reader is using one of
them: Bitwarden asked for the active tab after the reader moved to the
other and suggested a login for the page they had left.

QWebEngineExtensionManager::setSelectedPage takes the QWebEnginePage,
or the WebEngineView in Qt Quick, and is invokable from QML. From then
on that page is the browser window's active tab, to tabs.query and in
every tab an extension is told about, until the application selects
another, passes nullptr, or deletes the page. The manager holds the
page by a QPointer and finds its WebContents on each question, so a
deleted page is never answered and a page selected before it first
loads is found once it has. A page that is not one of the browser
window's tabs, an extension's popup or a window an extension opened,
is not answered. Without a selected page, the page on show answers as
before.
